<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    The Google G as the Google app draws it in its own search widget: one ring swept through the
    wallpaper palette, not the four brand colours. Hand-authored rather than run through
    design/convert-icons.sh, because the converter drops gradients and this one is the whole point.

    The sweep starts at 3 o'clock and runs clockwise, so the stops read crossbar, bottom, left, top.
    The stops, the paths and the palette roles in res/color and res/color-night come from the
    Google app's `super_g_dynamic_*` resources (17.66.12), not from sampling a screenshot. The
    crossbar cover is drawn flat over the ring's end so it reads as its own colour.
-->
